{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter","id":1555972,"title":"The Crimson Gutter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-30T02:16:20-08:00","id":1555972,"title":"The Crimson Gutter","content":"THE CRIMSON GUTTER is an interesting book and one that I am willing to give props to Renegade for creating even though I have my issues with it. Basically, The Crimson Gutter is a &quot;By Night&quot; city book without an actual city applied to it. It is a generic city book with a bunch of NPCs, locations, and plot hooks that can be applied to virtually any urban area. I've had that idea percolating in my brain for decades but always thought it had significant downsides. Does this game book overcome them?<br /> <br /> Not really. The Crimson Gutters is probably one of my favorite non-OPP Fifth Edition supplements after Blood Sigils but it's probably a three star, three star and a half book as my highest praise. The NPCs it creates for it's &quot;Anytown, USA&quot; are pretty generic. There's one who wants to be a Camarilla bigshot, a hypocritical Anarch, and a guy who just wants to use his second chance to be extremely rich. Yeah, those kinds of people. Inexplicably, they also don't provide a Prince, Baron, or Sheriff for the city.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the NPCs are the least interesting part of the book even though they're all fine. No, the biggest appeal of the game is that it is one of the rare WOD books that actually focuses on down and dirty street level gaming. The book presents the kind of adventures you must have when you are not going to be saving the world from Ur-Shulgi, Caine, or even likely to encounter the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> These aren't adventures that are particularly deep: one of them is a multi-chapter investigation of tracking down who is a local Kindred that has become a wight and then destroying him. Other adventures are figuring out who murdered a Church of Caine deacon, throwing a party for a visiting Archon, and impressing the various factions in the city enough to make them accept you as a member. It's the kind of low stakes gaming that works perfectly for the setting and we rarely get represented in the books.<br /> <br /> I like that the book also raises the Church of Caine to the level of the other two sects. I admit this is mostly because I like the Church of Caine as the Sabbat-lite and representing all of their intellectual religious side divorced from the ultraviolence. Also, able to have conversations with the other two sects. However, it also kind of falls into the trap that, &quot;If it was just back to the old ways, it'd be better.&quot; Still, the Church of Caine really was the best idea of Cults of the Blood Gods and I have no issue with its prominence in non-OPP work (take from the best).<br /> <br /> A nice bit is also the game actually provides some scenarios and scenes based around feeding. With all the attention V5 pays to feeding as a super important part of Kindred RPGing, this is one of the few books to actually provide interesting scenarios for Baggers, Alley Cats, Osirises, and so on. It also gives a lot of ideas for how to gain and lose domain in a city.<br /> <br /> Still, I feel like the book suffers from the fact that it is somewhat bloated describing fairly straight forward scenarios with twenty words when five would be fine. The NPCs are also slotted into the story when we don't really give them the kind of personalities that would make them stand out. I will give the writers credit for one thing, though: the NPCs have new sections where they list how the NPCs would be as the PC's sires and also what it would take to get the NPC to betray the PCs--which is perfect for vampire.<br /> <br /> So I rate it...okay.<br /> <br /> It is the unfortunate fact that I think Fifth Edition's design philosophy will never reach what it did under OPP. This is a matter of preference in that they were massive lore nerds the same as me (and still are for their own stuff) while these books seem deliberately designed to avoid lore as much as possible. Still, I've always felt that the gritty street level of 1st Edition was the best place for Vampire and I think OPP agreed since that was how they designed Requiem (and I may be giving them a bit too much credit here--though they deserve a lot--since that was always Requiem's thing). But if you have to pick up a supplement, I'd say Damnation City is probably a better choice for the same topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-30-2025, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T11:00:14-08:00","id":1555981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I've always felt that the gritty street level of 1st Edition </div> </div> </div>To believe that this was the ongoing tone of the comparatively short life first edition had is to basically say that nearly everything after the 1st corebook didn't exist, in first edition. 1st edition VtM had everything from vampire Louis Pasteur's Vampire cure, to the Chicago by Night that established the jyhad of warring Methuselahs, to Forged in Steel taking the coterie into city level political games, to the Actual Dungeon Crawl of Awakened: Diablerie, to a bunch of other things besides. The &quot;gritty street level of first edition&quot; was not sustainable or even slightly consistent, even in, first edition. That's just the nature of the actual existing material.<br /> <br /> This was part of 5th edition's problem, the early design process behind it was essentially a nostalgic fever dream of a time that didn't really exist outside of what was, in many ways, a fanon take on the setting, or more generously, people's personal campaigns that they liked and decided must mean how everyone else's were going. It otherwise required a belief that essentially 9 years worth of VtM books were almost all mistakes. That Vampire from the jump didn't contain multitudes, even though it clearly did. It also required warping what even &quot;gritty street level&quot; was supposed to mean to be able to say that somehow, whatever clearly wasn't, was anyway. At which point the words started to lose meaning in English.<br /> <br /> You can see that becoming an actual objective problem that finally caught up to them once 5th ed, after some years, basically ran out of ideas and has been for the last two or three doing all the things it mocked and said it would never do as regards the last several sourcebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 11-30-2025, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:02:01-08:00","id":1555989,"title":"","content":"I can't say for sure because I didn't actually read it, but...<br /> <br /> What it seems to me is that most of your problems with the book are simply because you're not its target audience.<br /> <br /> This looks like a good book for beginners by what you're saying. It gives an easy start VtM always had a problem with. Shallow characters are the best characters for someone who's still learning the ropes of STing, and this ST can give them the dept they need as they learn the game. This is a toolbox for a group that needs easy entrance and would feel overwhelmed by a full-fledged real city.<br /> <br /> You're too attached to lore in the sense that sometimes it isn't the point of a book. You should try to evaluate this book on how useful it is to an ST who needs a city they can use easily and tweak to their heart's content, because that's what it is, not about being a lore dump on this non-city city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:32:59-08:00","id":1555994,"title":"","content":"The one thing I remember about this book is that this is the one with the poor man's ersatz-Sabbat in the form of &quot;The Church of Caine&quot;. Making it a conflict between Camarilla, Anarchs and Sabbat felt like a more natural choice. And what Cults of the Blood Gods does with that faction is far more interesting than anything you get from this supplement, I think. So, in a way, I feel like you actually need to own Cults of the Blood Gods and this supplement to get the most out of that aspect of the book.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I think there's one bit of important context here. I posted about this in the past. There's a reason for why Crimson Gutter is about a generic city:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551245-somehow-white-wolf-returned?p=1551316#post1551316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate more on what the current approach towards WOD5E looks like, here\u2019s <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b8FNnDppMWo\" target=\"_blank\">an example Juhana Patterson (the current lead-developer of WOD5E) talked about</a>: This was at Ropecon 2023, a gaming-convention in Finland and so he talked about pitching a book like \u201cHelsinki by Night\u201d. WOD has city-books, even fifth edition does with a book like Chicago by Night. But if he were to pitch such a book these days, Paradox would flat-out refuse to greenlight this book. Doesn\u2019t matter how good the pitch is, they refuse to greenlight a book like that.<br /> <br /> Because the thinking goes: There needs to be one true canon in WOD5E. So, let\u2019s imagine they were to greenlight a book like that. Now there\u2019s a TTRPG book out there called Helsinki by Night, a V5 setting book about Helsinki. Next a videogame-developer approaches Paradox and says \u201cHey, I want to develop a VtM-game set in Helsinki.\u201d. And then Paradox will say \u201cBut the game has to align with this TTRPG-book.\u201d. The fear at the heart of this is that the videogame-developer will respond to that \u201cFuck that! Now I\u2019m not going to develop this videogame.\u201d And that\u2019s why they will simply refuse to greenlight any pitch with a realworld-location. That\u2019s why recently all the Renegade-releases use fictional locations instead. But on the flipside, when there\u2019s a videogame out there which uses a real-world-location, you have to acknowledge those games\u2019 setting and story-details in the TTRPG-books.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the &quot;generic-ness&quot; of this supplement is not there by choice. This is a result of restrictions that Paradox imposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:35:19-08:00","id":1555996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1555994#post1555994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I remember about this book is that this is the one with the poor man's ersatz-Sabbat in the form of &quot;The Church of Caine&quot;. Making it a conflict between Camarilla, Anarchs and Sabbat felt like a more natural choice. And what Cults of the Blood Gods does with that faction is far more interesting than anything you get from this supplement, I think. So, in a way, I feel like you actually need to own Cults of the Blood Gods and this supplement to get the most out of that aspect of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...it absolutely would not make any sense whatsoever to use the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I make the comparison of the three secrets myself but the Sabbat is at war with all other vampires and this is about three sects cohabitating more or less peacefully in the same city or engaged in a Cold War at worse.<br /> <br /> The book presents the Church of Caine as a group that does not value mortal life or traditional morality but want to evangelize to other vampires, not kill and diablerize them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:43:42-08:00","id":1555997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1555996#post1555996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean...it absolutely would not make any sense whatsoever to use the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I make the comparison of the three secrets myself but the Sabbat is at war with all other vampires and this is about three sects cohabitating more or less peacefully in the same city or engaged in a Cold War at worse.<br /> <br /> The book presents the Church of Caine as a group that does not value mortal life or traditional morality but want to evangelize to other vampires, not kill and diablerize them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book presents three &quot;quest-lines&quot; tied to one of the three factions in each case (in addition to a neutral introduction-chapter for the Chronicle). What's the problem with a Sabbat &quot;quest-line&quot;? I don't really understand the notion of &quot;absolutely make no sense&quot; here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T14:37:44-08:00","id":1556000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1555997#post1555997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the book presents three &quot;quest-lines&quot; tied to one of the three factions in each case (in addition to a neutral introduction-chapter for the Chronicle). What's the problem with a Sabbat &quot;quest-line&quot;? I don't really understand the notion of &quot;absolutely make no sense&quot; here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the set up is all three of these factions being ones the PCs can enjoy and existing beside one another. I guess my imagination is failing that the Sabbat can coexist with Anarchs and Camarilla like the Church of Caine can.<br /> <br /> My apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T14:48:51-08:00","id":1556001,"title":"","content":"The idea that V5 presents the Anarchs and Camarilla as coexisting with any consistency is an interesting take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T15:04:38-08:00","id":1556004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1556001#post1556001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that V5 presents the Anarchs and Camarilla as coexisting with any consistency is an interesting take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they did for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T15:27:42-08:00","id":1556006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1556004#post1556004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they did for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has taken a variety of opportunities to present them as, gently putting it, not doing so in the current setting. Being otherwise on the verge of outright violence, or actually engaging in outright violence, or at least engaged in low intensity lethal skirmishes, for as many times as they otherwise inhabit the same locale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T16:01:54-08:00","id":1556008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1556006#post1556006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 has taken a variety of opportunities to present them as, gently putting it, not doing so in the current setting. Being otherwise on the verge of outright violence, or actually engaging in outright violence, or at least engaged in low intensity lethal skirmishes, for as many times as they otherwise inhabit the same locale.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to note that Crimson Gutter is hardly the only V5 product to do so and I wonder if it was just bad communication in the initial takeaway versus the original plan:<br /> <br /> * New York in the visual novels and NYBN<br /> * Chicago by Night V5<br /> * LA By Night has the Camarilla and Anarchs briefly coexisting<br /> <br /> Milwaukee and London is really the only place where the Anarch are shown to be nonexistent while the same for Indianapolis in reverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T16:39:52-08:00","id":1556009,"title":"","content":"V5 having wild inconsistency in how it portrays some aspect of the game might as well at this point be a hallmark of V5. See the Second Inquisition for another example.<br /> <br /> But just on some specific notes..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LA By Night has the Camarilla and Anarchs briefly coexisting </div> </div> </div>Considering how LA By Night went down, that's a poor example of that really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chicago by Night V5 </div> </div> </div>Is hinted at the verge of open conflict given the Prince's &quot;Anarch List&quot; thing, and that at least one of the Anarch npcs rolled into down to do murders to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T16:53:22-08:00","id":1556010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1556000#post1556000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the set up is all three of these factions being ones the PCs can enjoy and existing beside one another. I guess my imagination is failing that the Sabbat can coexist with Anarchs and Camarilla like the Church of Caine can.<br /> <br /> My apologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused here... The whole point of Crimson Gutter's setup is for the players to join one of the factions. Eventually, you're supposed to make a choice and choose one faction. The book even offers advice on how the ST can <i>push </i>players to make that choice. <br /> <br /> That's why I think a Sabbat-option is completely acceptable here. The point is to present options in the first Act and then let the players decide which faction they want to support. Of course, I think it would be prudent to tell the players that this is a setup where you pick a faction and then you're stuck with that faction. Not that it has to go this way, of course, but you're gonna create<i> a lot of extra work</i> for the ST in question if you don't handle the Crimson Gutter-framework like that. <br /> <br /> And in that framework, offering the option where you help the Sabbat is completely acceptable. The point is that it's another option players can pick in what &quot;faction-quest-line&quot; they're gonna do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T23:57:05-08:00","id":1556086,"title":"","content":"I found this book a useful tool for character inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T06:41:34-08:00","id":1556142,"title":"","content":"Why do people seem to equate Sabbat and Church of Caine in V5? I thought the lore made a pretty big point that connection is firmly severed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27829-mallgoth","name":"Mallgoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T07:39:14-08:00","id":1556143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mallgoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555972-the-crimson-gutter?p=1556142#post1556142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do people seem to equate Sabbat and Church of Caine in V5? I thought the lore made a pretty big point that connection is firmly severed?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no connection whatsoever as far as I can tell other than some members are former Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Its really more thematic than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"lin